xline
=====

moo's line-editing module. Forked from isocline v1.1.0 by Daan Leijen
[https://github.com/daanx/isocline], licensed under the MIT License.
The upstream LICENSE file is preserved verbatim as `LICENSE.isocline`,
and every original source file retains its MIT copyright header.

Why a fork
----------

Upstream isocline is tiny, portable, pure-C, and permissively
licensed — an ideal starting point. We vendor it rather than consume
it as an external dependency so that we can:

  1. Integrate directly with moo's event loop (xLoop) — upstream
     only exposes a blocking `ic_readline()`; we need
     begin/step/end driven by our poller.
  2. Drop the `mem_t` / `alloc_t` indirection and use the standard
     allocator directly.
  3. Rename the public API (`ic_*`, `IC_*`) to moo's conventions
     (`xLine*`, `XLINE_*`).

Internal names (`ic_private`, `ic_env_t`, `ic_get_env`, …) are
intentionally kept upstream-style to minimise drift when
cherry-picking fixes from isocline.
